{
  "cells": [
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# Loading Pretrained Weights Notebook\n\n> Hands-on Build It and Exercises."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Build It"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "`code/main.py` implements:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "- A small replica of the lesson 35 `GPTModel` so this lesson is self contained."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "- `make_pretrained_to_local(num_layers)` which expands the per-layer entries."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "- `load_safetensors(model, path)` which iterates names, maps them, checks shape, transposes the conv1d-style weights, and assigns under `torch.no_grad()`. Returns a `LoadReport`."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "- `make_stub_safetensors(path, cfg)` which generates a fixture file with the exact pretrained naming convention."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "- A demo that creates `outputs/gpt2-stub.safetensors` on first run, builds a fresh model, captures one generated continuation from random init, loads the stub, captures another continuation, prints both, and verifies the two are different (the load actually changed the model)."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Run it:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```bash"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "python3 code/main.py"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Output: the fixture path, a per-name load log, a `LoadReport` summary, a continuation before the load, a continuation after the load, and a shape mismatch on a single intentionally bad tensor injected into the fixture so the failure path is exercised."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Exercises"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "1. Add a `dtype` argument to the loader that casts each tensor to a target dtype (`bfloat16`, `float16`, `float32`) during assignment. Confirm a `float32` model can be downcast to `bfloat16` and still generate.\n2. Add an `expected_layers` argument that refuses to load a checkpoint whose `h.N` indices do not match the model's `num_layers`.\n3. Plug the loader into the lesson 35 generation function and produce two side by side samples: one from random init, one from the loaded fixture.\n4. Add an export path: write the current model state into a fresh safetensors file using the pretrained naming convention. Round trip the loader and confirm the report has zero shape mismatches.\n5. Extend `NAME_MAP` to handle the LLaMA naming convention (no biases, RMSNorm, fused qkv layout) and re-run the loader on a stub LLaMA fixture you generate."
      ]
    }
  ],
